---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CaseStudy from '../../components/case/CaseStudy.astro';
import NotVerified from '../../components/case/NotVerified.astro';
import BookingFlow from '../../components/case/BookingFlow.astro';
import { projectRecords } from '../../data/portfolio';
import { sessionbook as sessionbookProject } from '../../data/registry';
import { sessionbookMeta, sessionbookBoundary } from '../../data/sessionbook';
import { SITE, caseMeta, SOCIAL_IMAGE } from '../../config/site';

const meta = caseMeta({
  name: sessionbookProject.name,
  summary: projectRecords.sessionbook.summary,
  image: '/social/sessionbook.png',
  imageAlt: 'SessionBook — a booking backend where the service, not the voice agent, decides what is true.',
});
const { title, description, image, imageAlt } = meta;
const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'CreativeWork',
  name: 'SessionBook',
  description,
  url: new URL('/work/sessionbook/', Astro.site).href,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.name },
  about: { '@type': 'SoftwareSourceCode', codeRepository: sessionbookMeta.repoUrl },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  {title}
  {description}
  {structuredData}
  {image}
  {imageAlt}
  imageWidth={SOCIAL_IMAGE.width}
  imageHeight={SOCIAL_IMAGE.height}
  ogType="article"
>
  <CaseStudy id="sessionbook">
    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <BookingFlow />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="problem">
      <p>
        A voice agent can ask what time works. It shouldn’t decide whether a slot exists, or
        whether someone just took it.
      </p>
      <div class="compare-grid">
        <div class="compare-sheet">
          <h3>The agent owns</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Transcription and turn-taking</li>
            <li>Prompting and the decision to call a tool</li>
            <li>Speech — how the answer is said</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-sheet compare-sheet--after">
          <h3>The backend owns</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Which slots are actually free</li>
            <li>Reserving one without double-booking</li>
            <li>Timezones, confirmation codes, what to say when it fails</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="contribution">
      <p>
        I built the FastAPI service behind that boundary: the tools the agent calls, availability
        queries, the booking transaction, the spoken responses.
      </p>

      <ul class="role-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Four HTTP tools</strong> — <code>get_today</code>, <code>check_availability</code>,
          <code>book_slot</code> and <code>confirm_booking</code>, mounted as
          <code>POST /tools</code> routes the agent calls itself.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The booking service</strong> — <code>app/services/booking_service.py</code>:
          availability, the locked booking transaction, confirmation codes and spoken labels.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The contracts and agent document</strong> — <code>schemas.py</code> bounds the
          request fields and validates phone numbers; <code>voice_agent/agent.json</code> points
          four tool definitions at the routes.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="case-note">
        AssemblyAI owns the conversation. SessionBook owns the agent document and the backend behind
        it. Nothing here streams or persists a socket.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="decisions">
      <dl class="decision-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Lock the slot before checking it</dt>
          <dd>
            <code>book_slot</code> takes <code>SELECT … FOR UPDATE</code> first, then checks the
            slot is still free. A unique constraint is the second line: the loser fails loudly.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Keep the clock provider-local</dt>
          <dd>
            Times are timezone-aware and spoken in Africa/Accra — the provider’s clock, not the
            caller’s.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Make the confirmation sayable</dt>
          <dd>
            Codes run six to ten characters with no 0/O or 1/I, and come with a spoken sentence so
            a caller can read them back.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Give failures something to say</dt>
          <dd>
            Failures come back as whole sentences — 409 “That slot was just taken, would you like
            another time?” — so the agent can ask again.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="result">
      <p>{projectRecords.sessionbook.result}</p>

      <dl class="case-states">
        <div>
          <dt>Implementation</dt>
          <dd>
            <strong>In source at commit 1264d9e.</strong> Four tool routes, a row-locking booking
            service, the contracts and the agent document.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Live calls</dt>
          <dd>
            <strong>Unverified.</strong> No call was made or replayed, and no deployment exists.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <p class="case-sub">In source</p>
      <ul class="case-evidence case-evidence--known">
        {sessionbookBoundary.known.slice(0, 3).map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="limits">
      <NotVerified
        lead="The repository verifies written implementation, not a working phone call."
        items={[
          ...sessionbookBoundary.missing,
          'Tool authentication has not been reviewed',
        ]}
        closing="Corrected here: an earlier version said short phone numbers passed validation. The service requires 7–15 digits."
      />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="sources">
      <ul class="case-sources">
        <li>
          <a href={sessionbookMeta.repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source repository</a>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">GitHub</span>
          <span>FastAPI service, agent configuration and setup notes.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${sessionbookMeta.repoUrl}/tree/${sessionbookMeta.repoCommit}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Source at {sessionbookMeta.repoCommit}
          </a>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">{sessionbookMeta.repoCommitDate}</span>
          <span>The commit this page was read against.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={sessionbookMeta.tutorialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            AssemblyAI HTTP tools tutorial
          </a>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">Reference</span>
          <span>Reference for the integration shape, not a SessionBook feature.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="case-note">
        No demo is linked. Setup instructions and an agent ID file don’t establish a deployment.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </CaseStudy>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .compare-sheet h3 {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-family: var(--font-instrument);
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-on-paper-faint);
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .compare-sheet ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
